orthant 1 language

-     - `coaxial.core` — the whole platform-neutral API: `Socket` (its `Backend`, `Option`s,
-       `Event`s, `Service` and `Error`), `Bind`, the typeclasses `Bindable`, `Connectable`,
-       `Routable`, `Serviceable`, `Duplexable` and `Subscribable`, `Duplex`, `Uds`,
-       `Multicast`, `Packet`, `UdpResponse`, `Control`, `Transmitter`, `Transmissible`,
-       `Ingressive`, the loans `listen`, `listenOn`, `subscribe`, `transmit`, `react`,
-       `exchange` and `duplex`, the `connectableSessional` given and the `socketOptions`
-       package. It compiles wherever a backend exists.
-     - `coaxial.jvm` — `socketBackends.javaBaseSockets` over `java.net` and
-       `java.nio.channels` (TCP, UDP, multicast and Unix-domain sockets), the TLS layer
-       (`Tls`, `TlsAcceptance`, `Trust`, `SecureEndpoint` for clients and `SecurePort` for
-       servers, with ALPN and mutual authentication), the raw-stream `Connection` with its
-       `listenConnections` loan, and `streamsDuplex`.
-     - `coaxial.native` (Scala Native) — `socketBackends.scalaNativeSockets` (TCP, UDP and
-       multicast; Unix-domain sockets raise `Unsupported`), and `Tls` and `SecureEndpoint` over
-       OpenSSL through its C API: a TLS client with verification but no ALPN, no server-side
-       TLS, and no `TlsAcceptance`/`Trust`.
-     - `coaxial.wasi` (a Wasm component) — `socketBackends.wasiSockets` over `wasi:sockets`:
-       TCP only, to IPv4 literals, with no UDP, multicast, Unix-domain or TLS; plus the
-       `wasiApis.wasiSocketsApi` WIT interface and the `WasiSocketsApi` type.
-     - `coaxial.dns` — `ask` on an `Endpoint[Udp.Port]`: one DNS message to a nameserver and
-       its answer, over the backend's one-shot datagram exchange.
+     - `coaxial.core` — l'intera API indipendente dalla piattaforma: `Socket` (il suo
+       `Backend`, le `Option`, gli `Event`, il `Service` e l'`Error`), `Bind`, le typeclass
+       `Bindable`, `Connectable`, `Routable`, `Serviceable`, `Duplexable` e `Subscribable`,
+       `Duplex`, `Uds`, `Multicast`, `Packet`, `UdpResponse`, `Control`, `Transmitter`,
+       `Transmissible`, `Ingressive`, i prestiti `listen`, `listenOn`, `subscribe`,
+       `transmit`, `react`, `exchange` e `duplex`, il given `connectableSessional` e il package
+       `socketOptions`. Compila ovunque esista un backend.
+     - `coaxial.jvm` — `socketBackends.javaBaseSockets` su `java.net` e `java.nio.channels`
+       (socket TCP, UDP, multicast e Unix-domain), lo strato TLS (`Tls`, `TlsAcceptance`,
+       `Trust`, `SecureEndpoint` per i client e `SecurePort` per i server, con ALPN e
+       autenticazione reciproca), la `Connection` a stream grezzo con il suo prestito
+       `listenConnections`, e `streamsDuplex`.
+     - `coaxial.native` (Scala Native) — `socketBackends.scalaNativeSockets` (TCP, UDP e
+       multicast; i socket Unix-domain sollevano `Unsupported`), e `Tls` e `SecureEndpoint` su
+       OpenSSL tramite la sua API C: un client TLS con verifica ma senza ALPN, senza TLS lato
+       server e senza `TlsAcceptance`/`Trust`.
+     - `coaxial.wasi` (un componente Wasm) — `socketBackends.wasiSockets` su `wasi:sockets`:
+       solo TCP, verso letterali IPv4, senza UDP, multicast, Unix-domain né TLS; più
+       l'interfaccia WIT `wasiApis.wasiSocketsApi` e il tipo `WasiSocketsApi`.
+     - `coaxial.dns` — `ask` su un `Endpoint[Udp.Port]`: un messaggio DNS a un nameserver e
+       la sua risposta, tramite lo scambio di datagrammi one-shot del backend.

